<http://taica.course/hw3/ontology> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology> .
<http://taica.course/hw3/ontology> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Vocabulary for HW3 Task 1 (semantic grounding + SHACL validation): robot specifications and FK/IK execution processes (the solvers themselves are implemented in Tasks 2-3) represented as machine-readable knowledge. Design rule: REUSE existing vocabularies wherever a suitable term exists — IEEE 1872 CORA for robots, SOMA for joints / joint states / poses, IEEE 1872 POS for positions, QUDT for units — and mint hw3: terms only for course-specific concepts (kinematic computations, D-H parameters, statuses, distances) that no standard vocabulary covers."@en .
<http://taica.course/hw3/ontology> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "TAICA HW3 Robot Kinematics Evaluation Ontology"@en .
<http://taica.course/hw3/ontology> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionInfo> "2026-fall-3.1" .
